Patch 2907 (experiment line): GPU_OVERLAP=1 lets the CPU build frame N+1 while the GPU still draws frame N.
render_frame began with a full wait for the GPU, so on a slow GPU a frame cost CPU build time + GPU time. With the
switch: that wait is skipped (move_to_next_frame still keeps one frame in flight), the per-draw SRV windows are
doubled by frame parity, resources the previous frame may use go through the grave, a slot upload buffer is waited
for before reuse. Off by default.

Tested (US disc, Training fight, integrated GPU): 27.38 -> 28.14 flips/s, picture unchanged, no readback waits; a fast discrete GPU 29.93.

